# {{META_REPO_NAME}}

<!-- HELIX:BEGIN overview -->
This is a Helix coordination meta repo.

It owns coordination artifacts only:

- repo registry in `helix-repos.yml`
- workspace artifacts in `workspaces/`
- Helix runtime state in `.helix/`
- Helix-managed docs, scripts, and templates in `helix/`
- Copilot runtime-facing files in `.github/`

It does not own product code. Product repos are attached from the registry only when a workspace needs them.

## Start Here

1. Update `helix-repos.yml` with the repos Helix can use.
2. Seed or edit `workspaces/<workspace-id>/workspace.yml`.
3. Run workspace setup.
4. Validate the install.
5. Start the Helix agents from this meta-repo root.

First workspace from repo ids:

```powershell
.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace directeddebit -ReposCsv "repo-a,repo-b,repo-c" -CloneMissing
```

`-ReposCsv` creates `workspaces/<workspace-id>/workspace.yml` only when it is missing. It validates repo ids against `helix-repos.yml`, infers role and branch from the registry, and then continues through normal workspace setup. If the workspace manifest already exists, edit it directly and rerun:

```powershell
.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace directeddebit -FetchExisting
```

Validate:

```powershell
.\helix\scripts\doctor.ps1
```

Setup is ready when `.helix/active-workspace.yml` points at the workspace, repo state exists under `.helix/repo-state/`, generated instructions exist under `.github/instructions/`, and `<workspace-id>.code-workspace` exists at the repo root.

## Common Scenarios

| Scenario | What to do |
|----------|------------|
| First setup after bootstrap | Fill `helix-repos.yml`, then run `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace <id> -ReposCsv "repo-a,repo-b" -CloneMissing` |
| Workspace manifest already exists | Edit `workspaces/<id>/workspace.yml`, then run `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace <id> -FetchExisting` |
| Add a repo to a workspace | Add it to `helix-repos.yml`, add its `repo_id` to `workspaces/<id>/workspace.yml`, then rerun setup |
| Switch active workspace | Run `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace <other-id> -FetchExisting` |
| Refresh repo state after branch or onboarding changes | Rerun `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1 -Workspace <id> -FetchExisting` |
| CRG bootstrap or repair | Run `.\helix\scripts\set-context-provider.ps1 -Provider code-review-graph -Mode mcp -Bootstrap`, then rerun setup |
| CRG is blocking urgent work | Run `.\helix\scripts\set-context-provider.ps1 -Provider code-review-graph -Mode off` as an explicit emergency fallback |
| Sync installed Helix files | Run `.\helix\scripts\sync-helix.ps1` |
| Validate current install | Run `.\helix\scripts\doctor.ps1` |

## When To Start Agents

Use `@setup` after the meta repo is bootstrapped and `helix-repos.yml` has real repos. The setup agent calls `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1`; it can pass `-ReposCsv` when you give repo ids, and otherwise expects `workspaces/<workspace-id>/workspace.yml` to already exist.

```text
@setup Set up workspace directeddebit, clone missing repos, refresh repo-state, and report readiness.
```

If the workspace manifest does not exist yet, include repo ids:

```text
@setup Set up workspace directeddebit with repos repo-a, repo-b, repo-c. Clone missing repos, refresh repo-state, and report readiness.
```

Use `@helix` after SETUP is complete:

```text
@helix Use active workspace directeddebit. Start JAM for: <feature idea>. Keep mode interactive.
```

Use the Ralph loop only after PRD, tech design, task breakdown, and a runnable execution plan exist:

```text
@helix Start Ralph loop for directeddebit using the current execution plan.
```

## CLI Commands

Future `helix` CLI commands and their current script equivalents:

| Future command | Current script |
|---|---|
| `helix sync` | `.\helix\scripts\sync.ps1` |
| `helix upgrade` | `.\helix\scripts\upgrade.ps1` |
| `helix workspace setup` | `.\helix\scripts\workspace-setup.ps1` |
| `helix doctor` | `.\helix\scripts\doctor.ps1` |

Until the `helix` CLI is available, invoke the scripts directly.

## Helix Docs

- `helix/README.md` — reusable Helix guide, setup scenarios, script reference, and agent handoff
- `helix/docs/helix-process.md` — canonical lifecycle, loops, and beta slice/verification model
- `helix/docs/helix-instance-schemas.md` — manifest shapes, validation rules, and beta runtime artifact schemas
- `helix/docs/helix-core-meta-repo-model.md` — packaging model for installed versus source layout
- `helix/docs/starting-cross-repo-feature-with-helix.md` — first cross-repo feature playbook

## Key Paths

- `.github/` — agents, prompts, skills, and Copilot instructions
- `helix/` — installed Helix-managed docs, scripts, and templates
- `.helix/` — install state, active workspace pointer, repo-state, generated state
- `.helix/context-providers.yml` — CRG mode and retrieval budgets (`off` is emergency fallback only)
- `.vscode/mcp.json` — VS Code project-level MCP server config (seeded once; preserved locally)
- `workspaces/` — feature-space artifacts, including task boards and decisions
- `helix-repos.yml` — canonical repo registry

> **Legacy:** `repos.yml` at the meta-repo root is a compatibility alias kept for older instances. New instances should use `helix-repos.yml`.

Legacy root `decisions/` and `task-boards/` directories are deprecated. Keep those artifacts under `workspaces/<workspace-id>/...`.
